ue\", \"name\": \"Pixel Pitch\", \"value\": \"0.9mm\"}, {\"@type\": \"PropertyValue\", \"name\": \"Brightness\", \"value\": \"1000 nits (peak 2000 nits HDR)\"}, {\"@type\": \"PropertyValue\", \"name\": \"Warranty\", \"value\": \"3 Years Standard | 5 Years Extended Available\"}]}10:Ta1b,{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What resolution does CinemaLED Ultra 0.9 offer?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"CinemaLED Ultra 0.9 delivers true 8K resolution with 7680x4320 pixels, ensuring ultra-high definition visuals ideal for the most demanding home cinema environments.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the pixel pitch and why is it important?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The pixel pitch is 0.9mm, which means pixels are placed very closely together. This tight spacing allows for sharp, detailed images that are perfect for close-range viewing in home cinema setups.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How bright is the CinemaLED Ultra 0.9 and does it support HDR?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"It offers 1000 nits brightness with a peak of 2000 nits for HDR content, supporting HDR10+ and Dolby Vision IQ for enhanced contrast and lifelike color accuracy.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What types of home cinema environments is this display suited for?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"This display is perfect for ultra-luxury home cinemas, superyacht theaters, and VIP screening rooms where immersive, high-end viewing experiences are required.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How does CinemaLED Ultra 0.9 compare to traditional projector-based home cinemas?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Unlike projectors, CinemaLED Ultra 0.9 provides infinite contrast through pixel-level dimming, 8K native resolution without scaling arti